course: dictionary
lesson: 1279
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and butch is one of them. Use the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits. «His nose became "nearly five feet long", and he said "This is too butch for me!"» The clue is the nose growing five feet long. The speaker means it is too much for them to handle, and butch is being used in a silly, playful way.
explain: The most common meaning is tough, strong and traditionally manly, as in «a butch dog» or «a butch name». These words sound tough, so they suggest strength. Butch is also a nickname, like the cowboy Butch Cassidy, and names like that start with a capital letter.
explain: Be careful, because butch is also slang for a lesbian woman who dresses or acts in a traditionally masculine way. Some women use it proudly about themselves. When other people use it, it can be rude or hurtful, so never use it to tease someone.
fact: Butch means tough, strong and traditionally manly, especially in informal talk.
fact: «A butch dog» means a tough-looking dog, and «a butch name» means a tough-sounding name.
fact: Butch Cassidy was an American outlaw in old westerns, and Butch is also a nickname.
fact: Butch is slang for a lesbian woman who dresses or acts in a traditionally masculine way. It can be a proud self-description, but used by others it can be rude.
fact: The kind rule is to use butch about a person only if they have chosen that word for themselves, and never to tease.
exercise: «A butch dog» is a dog that looks tough. What does butch mean here? | Soft and sleepy | Wet and grey | *Tough and strong | Very small and quiet
exercise: Butch Cassidy was a famous cowboy. Why does Butch start with a capital letter? | Because it is shouting | Because it is a rude word | *Because it is a name | Because it is the start of a sentence
exercise: Sam wants to tease a friend with butch. What is the kindest choice? | Shout butch at a stranger | Call a friend butch to make them laugh | Use butch about anyone who looks strong | *Only use butch about someone if they have chosen it for themselves
test: «This is too butch for me!» What does the speaker mean? | It is the best thing ever | It is very quiet | It is a dog's name | *It is too much for me
test: Butch is slang for which kind of person? | *A lesbian woman who dresses or acts in a traditionally masculine way | A petrol station attendant | A shop that sells meat | A cowboy in an old western
exam: Which statement is true? | Butch always means very old | *Butch can mean tough, and using it about a person can be rude or hurtful | Butch means a small, quiet dog | Butch is only ever a word for a cowboy
